{
  "title": "Timeout recovery doesn't check game_over after pass_priority",
  "description": "When an LLM request times out, `_handle_timeout` in \
`pilot_recovery.py` calls `pass_priority` to keep the game moving but \
doesn't check the response for `game_over` or `player_dead`. If the \
game ends while the timeout is being handled, the pilot loop continues \
and tries to call `choose_action` on a dead bridge, causing a \
`ToolExecutionError` that propagates as an `ExceptionGroup` crash.\n\
\n\
Evidence:\n\
- ~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260326_075453/MiMo Hist_pilot.log: line 708 \
(timeout at 08:42:07), line 713 (fatal \"Bridge processor is shut down\" after \
attempting choose_action post-game-over)\n\
- ~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260326_075453/MiMo Hist_errors.log: \"Fatal tool \
error: MCP tool choose_action failed: Bridge processor is shut down\"\n\
- Game ended at 08:42:19 via lethal combat while MiMo Hist was in timeout \
recovery\n\
\n\
Source: `src/magebench/pilot/pilot_recovery.py:131-134` — `pass_priority` \
result is discarded; `game_over`/`player_dead` not checked.\n\
\n\
Suggested fix: Parse the `pass_priority` response in `_handle_timeout` and \
return a signal (or raise) if `game_over`/`player_dead` is detected, similar \
to how `auto_pass_loop` checks at line 50-52.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "pilot",
  ],
